WEBVTT

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.210
Looks like you've done a lot of research,

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.460
but you seem to be struggling.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.970
Have you, perhaps, found a lead?

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.850
Anyway, my underlings reported to me

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:46.100
that they heard shrill noises coming 
from the document storeroom.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.490
It seems this mundane world 
plank is responsible.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.160
<b>Welcome
to the 
Modobashi 
Festival</b>

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.170
<b>Mystery 10 "The Messenger"</b>

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.170
Snooze

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.410
Break time's over.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.750
<i>Abeno-san said he'd come to school by noon.</i>

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.170
Ashiyan!

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.740
It's time.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.680
<b>Break Room!!</b>

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:38.890
Coming.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.580
Abeno-san!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.390
Abenon's here.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.480
Trick or treat!

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:58.990
Huh?

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.410
You're finally here.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.740
We've been waiting for you, Abeno.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.780
<i>Who is he?!</i>

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.410
<b>It's Saga</b>

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.920
<b>Modobashi Festival</b>

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.920
<i>He was late for the school festival.</i>

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.660
<i>Is he working in secret 
without telling me again?</i>

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:20.810
Don't worry. We got a costume for you, too.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.800
Time to get changed.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.620
You're not getting away, Abeno.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.940
Abenon, Abenon.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.860
<i>I'll ask him later.</i>

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.610
<b>Used Bookstore</b>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.360
<b><i>Magic Club</i></b>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.360
<b>Spot the Trick</b>

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.240
<b>Darts
 ¥100 Per Play</b>

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.750
Class 1-2 is running a Halloween café!

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.790
Come check it out!

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.370
Trick or treat...

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:57.240
Abeno-san, we're supposed to be advertising.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.040
You need to speak up.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.470
Shut up, witch. I'll harvest your soul.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.930
Sorry, Mr. Reaper.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:09.680
<i>This morose-to-the-max grim reaper 
shouldn't be interacting with customers.</i>

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.620
<i>Where are his yokai customer service skills?</i>

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.490
Welcome!

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:22.720
Our menu includes pumpkin smoothies, 
pumpkin fondue, and fried pumpkin!

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.760
I recommend the pumpkin coriander pie!

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.410
Could we not have picked more standard items?

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.480
Would you like some pumpkin? 
It prevents colds and keeps you warm!

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.750
A café promoted for its health benefits by 
a witch and grim reaper is beyond suspect.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.570
Stop complaining about my advertising 
when you're supposed to be helping!

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.590
You wanna fight?!

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.700
That witch and reaper are battling!

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.440
Is it a kendo club performance?

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.540
Stop fighting.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.980
I'm confiscating your weapons.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.200
Class 1-2's doing a Halloween café, huh?

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.400
You should stop by.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.240
Okay.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.610
Are you walking around by yourself, Zenko?

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.230
No, there's two of us.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.460
Yesterday, I accidentally 
mentioned the festival...

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:18.110
No! No, no, no!

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.920
I wanna play!

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.620
<i>He's throwing such a violent tantrum.</i>

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.370
I wanna go to the haunted house!

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:22.650
<i>It's so cute.</i>

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.510
I wanna eat ice cream!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:28.010
Take me with you, Zenko!

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.010
No.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.760
You'll get in trouble with Abeno if 
you go to school without permission.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.500
Haruitsuki's scary when he's angry.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.280
<i>Did he give up?</i>

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.600
I'll help you clean, Zenko.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.560
In that case, can you sweep the walkway?

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.340
Sure.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.200
<i>Not a single speck of dust 
escapes his tail broom.</i>

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.040
<b>Tail Broom</b>

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.920
Since I'm being a good boy, I can go 
to the cultural festival, right?

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:06.670
You still can't.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.580
What?! No, no!

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.400
I'm gonna make a cotton candy 
bigger than myself and roll it!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.560
I wanna swim in a pool of ice cream!

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:20.650
I wanna chase the ghosts out of the 
haunted house and scare the humans!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.690
That's exactly why you can't go.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:29.440
That prankster Yahiko came to 
this school-turned-playground?

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:31.820
So you brought him.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.950
Should I not have?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.730
So where is Yahiko?

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:41.290
Well... we were just separated in the crowd.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.300
He's lost?

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.590
He wouldn't get lost.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.320
If he wanted to find Zenko,

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.030
he'd be able to find her 
by her smell or presence.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:54.720
But he came to school suppressing his 
presence so neither I nor Ashiya would notice.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:58.820
He's a fugitive who came with every 
intention of goofing off on his own.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.560
<i>There's no way nothing will happen!</i>

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.570
We need to catch Yahiko!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.960
There's a place Yahiko wanted to go.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:07.940
Where?

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.200
<b>Bloodcurdling Hospital Ward
</b>Bloody Ghosts Tonight

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.200
Here.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.680
A haunted house, huh?

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.820
Next... three patients... please...

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.060
come inside.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.760
Stop!

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:46.350
I was super moved at the end.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:47.650
Yeah.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.440
A happy ending at a haunted 
house is such a buzzkill.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.090
Did you guys even look for Yahiko?

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.580
Did you see Yahiko?

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.540
He hadn't transformed himself into anything.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:01.310
Where else would Yahiko go?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.790
<b>Soft Serve Ice Cream</b>

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.790
Welcome.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.130
One ice cream, please.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.760
Here you go.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.000
What?!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.900
The tip disappeared?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.840
Why?

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.890
Hooray! Cultural festivals are fun!

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.210
There are so many tasty sweets!

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.970
That crêpe is flying!

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.970
There are so many places to play, too!

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:24.980
It's not fair for humans to have all the fun!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.020
Where should I go next?

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:29.900
You're...

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.030
I sense Fuzzy sending me a signal.

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.800
Did he find Yahiko?

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.040
We were right to call the hairball.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:49.170
Yahiko is wherever Fuzzy is!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.920
Let's go, Ashiya. Don't let him escape.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.170
Yes, sir!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:56.420
Let go! I can't play like this!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:58.890
Ashiya?

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:04.430
H-Haruitsuki...

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:12.380
Naughty.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:13.740
I'm sorry.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.820
Haruitsuki, let's play!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.950
What? You don't seem very remorseful.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.910
Thanks to Yahiko running around wild...

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:27.250
Some darts suddenly flew at the 
board and earned a high score!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.380
I jammed with a ghost drummer!

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.700
The brush started moving on its own

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:35.420
and drew a bright red 
shape on a blank canvas!

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.880
Go back to the temple before 
you cause any more commotion.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.180
What?!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.180
I don't wanna!

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.310
Go home.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.930
No!

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:46.600
No, no, no, no, no!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:50.860
Yahiko's even more willful than normal today.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:52.110
No, no, no, no, no!

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:56.610
No, no, no, no, no!

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:56.610
I wasn't going to bring him, but...

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.370
Fine. I won't go to the cultural festival.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.490
I hate cultural festivals.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.300
Yahiko?

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.750
Humans are mean.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:14.500
It's not fair that humans 
get to have all the fun.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.560
We live in the mundane world, too.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.260
Why do we have to hide quietly?

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.140
Yahiko...

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.390
I don't care anymore.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:26.150
I'll hang out in Okina's forest tomorrow.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.850
What do you want for your snack tomorrow?

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:32.970
Kinako mochi and hot cocoa!

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.320
I don't have kinako mochi or hot cocoa.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.570
Aw...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.820
Then what should I have instead?

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:46.330
But tomorrow, there'll be crêpes, 
ice cream, and cotton candy.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.960
Let's go to the cultural festival together.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:55.520
I didn't really think about it.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.090
It's not fair, huh?

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.630
Yahiko, let's go home.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:04.170
You shouldn't cause trouble 
for Abeno and Ashiya.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.100
Abeno-san?

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:16.860
Fine. I'll play with you.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.720
But not here.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.040
Let's go someplace where 
there are no people.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.040
Okay!

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.570
Let's go to Okina's place!

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:42.010
I'll go get changed. You head there.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:42.970
Okay!

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.170
Let's race to see who's faster,
me or the Mononokean!

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:49.020
See you later!

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.150
Abeno, are you finished 
working at the festival?

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:58.530
My job involves yokai, so yokai come first.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:02.400
This human bullhorn should be able to 
handle promoting the café by himself.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.280
Leave it to me!

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:09.770
Can I take a picture of you 
guys as a witch and reaper?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.730
Sure!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.160
No.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.620
I win.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:36.730
Shucks. I ran as fast as I could.

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.280
Want to play?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.230
I'm tired. I'm taking a break.

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:48.490
Yahiko.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.370
Do you know a human named "Ashiya Sakae"?

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:55.990
Ashiya?

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:59.380
I know him. It's Ashiya, right?

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.300
Not the five-year-old. Ashiya Sakae.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.330
Huh? I don't get it.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.580
Ashiya, not Ashiya?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.250
Ashiya, not Ashiya?

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.000
I phrased my question poorly.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:18.430
He was a human who could see yokai, 
who most likely unofficially and secretly

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.680
worked for the Mononokean.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:24.150
A man with blond hair and golden 
eyes who worked with Aoi.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:29.370
But he may have dyed his hair 
and worn color contacts.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.160
We can't rely on his appearance.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:34.620
Sixteen years ago...

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:38.890
By your sense of time, 
it should be about sixty years.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:43.830
He died for some reason,

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.390
the year Ashiya was born.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:52.680
<i>Which means the father Ashiya 
met when he was three...</i>

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.220
Maybe you mean him.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:58.490
Him?

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:03.580
If you play with me until I'm satisfied,

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.540
I'll transform into him.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.630
Trick or treat!

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:15.020
Class 1-2 is running a Halloween café!

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.830
Come check it out.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.210
Trick or treat.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.900
Isn't that costume too big for you?

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:26.330
No. I feel bad that Yahiko 
ruined the festival for you.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.470
I should at least fill in for Abeno.

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:33.850
He was even enjoying dressing up for once.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:40.550
He'd want me to tell you he wasn't 
having fun being a grim reaper.

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:41.730
But...

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:45.080
Despite what he thinks, it suited him.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:45.980
Yeah.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:49.960
<i>A reaper...</i>

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:52.860
<i>Back then...</i>

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:05.550
<i>Back then, since he showed 
up in the white snow,</i>

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.090
<i>he looked like Santa Claus to me.</i>

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.720
<i>But now that I think about it,</i>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.310
<i>he looked less like Santa 
Claus and more like</i>

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.660
<i>a grim reaper.</i>

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.600
Trick or treat.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.730
Trick or treat!

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.700
Haruitsuki, let's play hide-and-seek again!

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.600
Isn't three hours enough?

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.450
What?

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.580
It'll be dark soon. Zenko will be worried.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.080
Fine. I'm going home.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.230
Didn't you promise you'd do something first?

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:48.300
Promise? Oh, right.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.140
I'm supposed to transform into him.

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:02.730
Ta-da! He looked something like this.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.820
Welcome back.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.450
So you weren't at school.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.960
I was playing with Yahiko in the forest.

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.830
<i>That human...</i>

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:29.340
<i>That's Ashiya Sakae, Ashiya's father.</i>

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:34.590
<i>A school uniform?</i>

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:39.600
When I went to play with 
Aoi, this guy was there.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.100
I think he said his name,

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.810
but I forgot it.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.430
Do you know if he died?

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.460
No idea.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:57.050
I don't bother to keep 
track of whether humans

00:16:57.050 --> 00:17:00.490
who don't play with me are still alive.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.550
Hey, I remember now!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:08.000
When I asked him who he was,

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.940
he said he was an employee 
of the Mononokean.

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:16.010
<i>Ashiya Sakae was an employee?</i>

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:22.680
<i>I searched all the records, 
but I didn't find any account of him.</i>

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.620
<i>So they hid it from the Legislator 
and the Mononokean itself?</i>

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.900
Komon-sama came while you were gone.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.560
Komon-dono?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.740
Komon-sama came while you were gone.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.740
Komon-dono was here?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:43.790
Yes. He's finally able to hire us.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:45.350
Got it.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.290
Several Days Later

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.920
Fuzzy!

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:56.670
Mononokean, you put the 
exit in the wrong spot.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:00.390
Oh, really? Should I have 
put it farther to the right?

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.310
You can do it, Fuzzy!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.720
Almost there! Almost there!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.110
That's it! You're almost there!

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.510
Huh?

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:18.200
Was that...

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.970
Fuzzy!

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:23.950
Abeno-san! A bird took Fuzzy!

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.640
Fuzzy is... Fuzzy is...

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.070
That was no ordinary bird.

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:29.160
Huh?

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.410
That was probably...

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.460
Once again, I'm opening a door 
to Komon-dono's residence.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:36.990
Komon-san?

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:38.710
Today's client.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.880
We're in the right place this time, right?

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:48.780
Yeah.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:52.090
It's a cliff. You'll die if you fall.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:54.280
Now you tell me!

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:13.710
These cries...

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:15.920
Pardon the intrusion.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:19.880
Abeno-san! You shouldn't make such 
bold moves at the top of a cliff!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.260
Hairball, you okay?

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:31.770
Looks like some of your hair's 
been plucked to build a nest.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:32.650
But you're okay.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.650
Hey! How could you?!

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.580
Fuzzy's beautiful hair!

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.980
Hey! Don't push me! I'll fall!

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.990
What happened, fellas?

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:45.610
What? There are humans at my doorstep.

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:47.240
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.320
Remember what I told you.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:54.040
Humans can't see or hear us.

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:59.880
Watch this. I'll drive them away by 
throwing the chestnuts I picked at them.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.260
Komon-dono!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.010
Huh?

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.760
It's good to see you again!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.390
I'm Abeno of the Mononokean!

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:09.080
What? The Mononokean?

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:12.100
That yokai is our client?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.960
Abeno of the Mononokean?

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:18.760
Right! I recognize that blond hair.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:22.730
You're the human employee 
of the Mononokean, Itsuki.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:23.590
Yes.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:27.220
<i>Abeno-san, an employee?</i>

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:31.370
I handled the request you made that one time.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.260
<i>This job is from when 
Abeno-san was an employee.</i>

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:40.360
<i>Which means... when Aoi-san was the master.</i>

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:51.460
Itsuki, I appreciate you remembering 
the request I made that day.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:57.500
Now that's a problem. 
They can't be exorcised, huh?

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.600
<i>We can't exorcise them</i>

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:08.410
<i>because they're too weak to acclimate 
to the environment in the Underworld.</i>

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:10.910
Then it can't be helped.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.910
Now that I've taken them in, 
I can't abandon them.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:18.420
I'll take care of them until they're 
strong enough to be exorcised.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:22.660
What should we do, Aoi?

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:29.050
That's fine, but be careful you 
don't take too good care of them.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:34.820
Please contact us again once 
they're ready to be exorcised.

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:46.820
Let's return to the Mononokean, Itsuki.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:52.010
Okay.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time: "The Return"</b>

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:29.090
This time we've been hired 
to exorcise quintuplets,

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:33.130
but for some reason, one of them can't fly.

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:35.050
Next time, "The Return."

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:38.140
It seems like there's some reason for it.
